@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About";
}

<div class="page-head">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>What this app does</p>
</div>

<div class="prose">
    <p>
        Weather Seeker reads live conditions and a five-day outlook from
        <a href="https://openweathermap.org/api" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">OpenWeatherMap</a>
        and lays them out as a single console. Search a city, or use the location button to read the
        station nearest you.
    </p>

    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Forecast lookups are proxied through this server, so the weather API key is never sent to a browser.</li>
        <li>Readings are cached for ten minutes, which keeps repeat views fast and stays inside the free API tier.</li>
        <li>The five-day strip shows each day's high and low; the trace above it is drawn from the same numbers.</li>
        <li>The converter on the console turns Celsius into Fahrenheit as you type.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Accounts</h2>
    <p>
        The console requires a session. New accounts can be created as a client; admin accounts are
        issued only by an existing admin. Passwords are stored as one-way hashes — never as plain text.
    </p>
    <p>
        Use a disposable username and a unique password. See the
        <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Privacy">privacy page</a> for what is stored.
    </p>
</div>
